WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.190
Speaker 1: I just absolutely love this story
I'm starting with today.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:09.630
Colorado election officials are formally ordering
a recount in Lauren Boebert congressional

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:14.070
race, which she won by five 550 votes against
challenger Adam Fresh.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.660
Now, if you look at the reporting, they say
very clearly this is not expected to change

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.540
the result.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.730
But this is so fascinating because these people
on the right who just insist everything's

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.650
stolen, recount everything, audit everything,
blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.600
Now, there is actually a legitimate reason
for a recount to be ordered in a race that

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.520
Lauren Boebert is, of course, extraordinarily
relieved to have survived because she almost

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.480
went down after just one term in Congress
to Adam French.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.890
So there's an article from the Colorado Sun
and it says Colorado elections officials formally

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.060
order recount in race between Lauren Boebert
and Adam Frisch.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.239
Boebert leads fresh, who has already conceded
by 550 votes.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:01.150
The recount is not expected to change the
outcome of the third congressional district

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.670
race.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:09.520
This is a mandatory recount and it was expected
this was a closely watched race.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.770
Boebert leads fresh.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:16.880
The margin is 550, but the law is that you
must have a mandatory recount when the number

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.479
of votes separating the two leading candidates
is less than half of a percentage point of

00:01:23.479 --> 00:01:33.540
the number of votes cast, the margin is 0.3%,
meaning that the recount must take place.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.869
The secretary of State, Janet Griswald, who's
a Democrat, added the results of the District

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:41.340
three race reinforce the fact that every vote
matters.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.229
Colorado voters have made their voices heard.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:46.700
I'm ordering the recount in accordance with
Colorado law.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.479
This can begin immediately.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:53.790
Recounts rarely shift the major margin beyond
a few votes, which is why Fresh conceded in

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.790
the closer than expected contest.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.670
The third district leans heavily in Republicans
favor.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.060
This is this is just great.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.090
So I don't think it will change the outcome.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.810
I believe Lauren Boebert really won.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.509
This is still a fascinating race because as
the article points out, that third district

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:13.770
in Colorado is quite a right leaning district.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:20.230
And the fact that it came down to 0.3 between
an incumbent Republican member of Congress,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:26.930
Lauren Boebert, and the challenger Adam Frisch,
means that MAGA really isn't safe.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.280
And we saw Madison Cawthorn defeated and removed
from the House of Representatives.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.769
We'll talk about him in the next segment and
his crazy outgoing speech.

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:41.730
But there is a real question as to the viability
of MAGA going into 2024 and just making Lauren

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:46.500
Boebert have to wait a little bit longer is
a really great thing that I can certainly

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.500
get behind.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:54.599
Now, when it comes to 2024, we still don't
know what is going to be the level of strength

00:02:54.599 --> 00:02:56.040
of these MAGA candidates.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:01.890
I think it will be different if Donald Trump
remains in the race and becomes the nominee

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:07.390
versus if Trump remains in the race but loses
the nomination, versus if Donald Trump simply

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.750
bails on the primaries because it's looking
so terribly.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.110
We don't know which of those three scenarios
ultimately will happen.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:20.500
But if it's the ones that are not so good
for Trump, this may be it for these MAGA people.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:27.569
We will be years removed from MAGA in November
of 2024 and it would be great if people like

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:34.090
Boebert were removed and ended up being just
sort of a blip in American political history.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.549
Cawthorn was removed, Marjorie Taylor GREENE
won easily.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:41.819
Lauren Boebert won, but by a very small margin.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:43.670
Let's hope it keeps going in that direction.

